          FIG 1A BOOTSTRAP CIRCUIT





EECS BOOTSTRAP
VDD 5 0 -75
V2  3 0 -15
V1  1 0 -21 0U  -21 10U 0 20U 0 500U
Q1 M1 4 1 0 0 200MU 38MU   0 0 4000 4000
Q2 M1 5 2 4 0 100MU 38MU   0 0 4000 4000
M3 M1 3 1 2 0  80MU 38MU   0 0 160   160
M1 PMO VTO=-1 VOX=34.5N
+ XN=9MU UB=164 GDS=2 CJUN=.0006P
CS 2 4 15P
CL 4 0 10N
PLOT V1 1 0 V4 4 0
END



          FIG 1B   MSINC INPUT DATA
	Instructions for using MSINC at CMU

The files for MSINC are currently stored on [c390rs40]/A: MSINC.DOC
(this file), MSINC.SAV (runable file), sources may be there as well.
The program has been modified to prompt for names of input and output
files.  Names should be at most 5 characters; extensions should be
.DAT.  When asked for a name, simply type the five-character name.  A
helpful convention is to name the input (source) file xxxxI.DAT, and
the corresponding output file xxxxO.DAT.

Unfortunately, the output file contains line printer control
characters in the first position of each line.  The file can be
re-formatted suitable for listing by invoking:

	.R PIP
	*xxxxO.DAT=xxxxO.DAT/C/P
	*^C
	.LIST xxxxO.DAT

␀